<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67052" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετα-χρόνιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		poet. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνος</span>) prop., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετάχρονος</span>
			, <i>happening afterwards</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Tryph.
				1
			</span></i>; of an oracle <i>post eventum</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				28
			</span></i>; <i>delayed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.522
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετέωρος</span>
			, <i>high in air</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταχρόνιαι</span>
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γὰρ ἴαλλον [Ἅρπυιαι</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				269
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.300
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pae.Oxy.</u>
				660.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				20.289
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				42.1
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταχθόνιος</span> is suggested
			in Sch.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.587
			</span></i>; but Gramm. recognize this use of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταχρόνιος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταίσιον</span>
			 (leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετάρσιον</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
			</span></i><i>Lex.,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				EM
				581.41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i></div>
